{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406630-\u200bulfire-jel-the-radiance-forbidden-eighth-soul-of-the-dragon-beyond-the-world","id":1406630,"title":"\u200bUlfire Jel, The Radiance Forbidden, Eighth Soul of the Dragon Beyond the World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-06T07:05:28-07:00","id":1406630,"title":"\u200bUlfire Jel, The Radiance Forbidden, Eighth Soul of the Dragon Beyond the World","content":"<b>Ulfire Jel, The Radiance Forbidden, Eighth Soul of the Dragon Beyond the World</b><br /> <br /> Within Malfaes is a temple, where the priests of Ceclyne avert their eyes for within it's walls there is none of the sacred cerulean. It's walls are painted in red-green, the columns in yellow-blue. The altar is draped in stygian crimson, and the monks wear magenta robes. They paint and seek to capture the unattainable beauty of Ulfire Jel, the Radiance Forbidden, but they strive without success for they are all the colors not seen.<br /> <br /> Where Ulfire Jel is, her impossible light conceals and reveals at once. Those unaccustomed to her presence are easily dazzled, their senses overwhelmed as the strange radiation rings in their ears or lays upon their tongue like smoking metals. Those familiar can see how the subtle shift of rej in the eyes and ultracitrines and infraviolaceous of their face revealing hidden thoughts and secret plans. Where they leave, they take all colors with them, leaving the world drab and washed out, as if shroud in perpetual fog-draped gloom, and becomes an abode of unhealthsome things.<br /> <br /> They were rarely summoned; although their presence allowed the shaping of Creation as the depths of Wyld, their nature is too inimical for the world to easily bear. Even now, thousands of years since the Radiance Forbidden last shown upon Creation; the palace she decorated (although rich in furnishings and with tall, proud towers) stands hollow and empty. No law forbids entrance; no law is necessary to bar that grey place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T08:25:08-07:00","id":1406637,"title":"","content":"Is this that thing Nicolas Cage fought in a movie last year? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bDon't know that I'll ever use this, but this is probably one of the better H.P. Lovecraft references you could make in Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200b(A bit of writing advice - &quot;it's&quot; is a contraction of &quot;it is.&quot; &quot;Its&quot; with no apostrophe is the one you want to use.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date